# WHAT IS BINARY, SAID OUT LOUD.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the machine this was built on, and git decides whether
# to rewrite a file's line endings by looking for a NUL byte in its first 8000. That
# heuristic is right for most things and wrong for some: the 49-page roster PDF has
# no NUL in its first 8000 bytes, so git announced it would convert LF to CRLF in it
# - which would have committed a corrupted copy of the only copy there was, on the
# day the machine holding the original was wiped.
#
# A backup that silently mangles what it stores is worse than no backup, because it
# looks like one. So the formats are named rather than sniffed.
*.pdf    binary
*.aseprite binary
*.ase    binary
*.glb    binary
*.gltf   binary
*.blend  binary
*.blend1 binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.bin    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.mp3    binary
*.wav    binary
*.ogg    binary
*.ply    binary
*.exr    binary
